From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 15:12:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Close the discovery gap: pin-down's missing banner, and the
 Library card's flat "Enabled" badge
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two real gaps found in this session's own follow-up review of the
post-onboarding discovery experience — see the conversation's own
analysis: a green "Enabled" badge looked identical whether a worker was
fully configured or completely broken, which is the exact "I'll finish
it later, it feels optional" trap this whole plan exists to close,
reappearing one level up from where it was already fixed for the
onboarding worker itself.

- pin-down-config-form.tsx: its own bridge GET route already computed and
  returned `enabled` (isSkillEnabledForEngagement), same as icp-lock's
  and rep-onboarding's routes — but the form never read it, so a disabled
  Pin-Down showed no indication of that on reopening its setup screen.
  Now shows the same "currently turned off, saving turns it back on"
  banner the other two already have.

- worker-capability-status.ts: new getWorkerCompletenessSummaries(),
  a server-side batch version of the same read the Live Capability Matrix
  already does per-worker, for every worker on a Library page in one
  Promise.all instead of N client round trips.
- library/[product]/page.tsx: fetches it alongside everything else this
  page already loads, passes it down as a plain serializable object.
- product-detail-client.tsx: threads it through to each WorkerCard.
- worker-card.tsx: the "Enabled" badge (both the row and card variants —
  only row is actually rendered anywhere today, but both were the same
  bug) now shows amber "Enabled — needs setup" with a real active/total
  tooltip when a worker is on but incomplete, instead of the same flat
  green either way. Falls back to today's plain badge for the ~20 workers
  with no WORKER_CAPABILITIES data (nothing real to say) or when there's
  no active engagement yet.

Also checked, not fixed: the engagement detail page's own WorkersPanel
(a separate implementation, doesn't reuse WorkerCard) already derives its
status from real run outcomes (not_run/live/failed), so it doesn't have
the same falsely-reassuring-green problem — but "not_run" is still
ambiguous about whether that's just "hasn't fired yet" or "would fail
immediately on missing config." Smaller, different-shaped version of the
same underlying gap, left for a follow-up rather than expanding this
pass's scope unilaterally.

tsc clean, vitest unchanged at the established baseline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QVWhaC6hTtT9UCKS7Dub7w
