Subject: [PATCH] Close the not_run ambiguity in the engagement page's Skills
 panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Same underlying gap as the Library card's flat "Enabled" badge, one
level deeper: a worker that had never fired showed the identical
"not_run" swatch whether that meant "fine, just hasn't happened yet"
or "would fail the instant it tried, because a required field is
blank." Now checked against worker-config-completeness.ts's own
getMissingRequiredFields — the exact gate inngest/skill.ts itself runs
before every dispatch, not a new parallel check — so this can't
disagree with what would actually happen on the next real run. Costs
nothing extra for the 20 zero-config workers (no CHECKERS entry
resolves to [] with no DB call).

- worker-config-completeness.ts's missing-field list is now fetched
  server-side per enabled worker on the engagement page and passed
  down as missingFieldsByWorkerId.
- deriveModuleStatus returns a new "needs_setup" status distinct from
  "not_run", only for the first-run case — a worker with real run
  history already has better evidence (its last run either worked or
  didn't), so this doesn't touch failed/live/running at all.
- The card shows which fields are missing, by label, both in the
  status swatch's tooltip and inline where "No executions yet." used
  to be the only message.

Checked, not touched: the engagement-list page's own client-roster-table.tsx
has the identical ambiguous not_run derivation, but nothing imports it —
dead code, not worth carrying this fix into. The dashboard's live
execution feed and queue panel, and the run detail page, all operate on
real run rows only and have no per-worker completeness concept to begin
with — genuinely unaffected, not just unexamined.

tsc clean (same 5 pre-existing unrelated test-file errors as baseline),
vitest unchanged at 59 failed/210 passed/18 skipped.

